BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Gridiron Glove) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY: GRIDIRON GLOVE) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Youth football is a very large activity in America with millions of kids playing every fall,) Tj T* (and wide receivers are one of the most technique dependent positions on the field. Catching the) Tj T* (ball with the hands instead of the body, hand position, and timing of the finger close are all) Tj T* (things that can be taught but only if somebody is watching and giving feedback. The problem is) Tj T* (that most youth and middle school football programs are run by volunteer coaches who have a) Tj T* (full roster of kids, limited practice time, and often no specific background in receiver play.) Tj T* (High schools and colleges can use video analysis software and have assistant coaches for each) Tj T* (position group, but youth programs mostly can not afford this. As a result bad habits like body) Tj T* (catching and late hand closure are formed early and stick with players for years. Coaches we) Tj T* (talked to \(about 14 so far, mostly from rec leagues and two middle schools near our university\)) Tj T* (told us this is one of their biggest frustrations, and several said they would pay for a tool) Tj T* (that tells them what to fix.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Gridiron Glove is a training glove with embeded sensors paired with a mobile application. The) Tj T* (glove has pressure sensors in the palm and fingertips plus a small motion sensor on the back of) Tj T* (the hand. When a player catches a ball the glove records the contact pattern and the timing and) Tj T* (the app converts that into a catch technique score from 0 to 100. The score breaks down into) Tj T* (sub scores such as hand placement, finger closure timing, and whether the ball was secured with) Tj T* (hands only or trapped to the chest. After a practice session the app shows the coach a simple) Tj T* (team dashboard, ranks players, and suggests specific drills from a library tied to each) Tj T* (weakness. The coach does not need to review video or understand biomechanics. Our software is) Tj T* (designed to be simple enough to use on a phone at the field while kids are doing reps.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our prototype currently works with one glove size and a wired connection to a small battery) Tj T* (pack and our scoring is based on rules we developed with advice from two coaches rather than a) Tj T* (large data set. Wireless and multiple sizes are on the roadmap.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (According to widely cited industry figures there are several million youth tackle and flag) Tj T* (football players in the United States and hundreds of thousands of youth teams. If even a small) Tj T* (fraction of these teams bought a set of gloves, this would be a meaningful market. We estimate) Tj T* (the total addressable market at over one billion dollars by multiplying the number of players) Tj T* (by an assumed price, though we realize that not every player needs their own glove. Our more) Tj T* (realistic serviceable market is youth leagues and middle school programs that already spend) Tj T* (money on equipment, which we think is roughly 20 to 30 thousand programs. Our first target is) Tj T* (the region around our university where we have relationships with a number of leagues, and then) Tj T* (expanding state by state.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to sell a team kit of 6 gloves with the software included for the first year, priced) Tj T* (around 450 dollars, and then charge an annual software subscription of about 120 dollars per) Tj T* (team after that for the dashboard, drill library and updates. We also plan to sell single) Tj T* (gloves to parents and individual players at roughly 99 dollars, and to sell to private receiver) Tj T* (training camps. Our cost to build each glove at prototype stage is around 38 dollars in parts,) Tj T* (and we believe this could fall at volume but we have not gotten manufacturing quotes yet.) Tj T* (Longer term we see revenue from league wide licensing deals and from data insights, though the) Tj T* (data side is early thinking.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
