BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (There are video analysis platforms used by high school and college programs, but these are) Tj T* (expensive and need cameras and staff time. There are also smart ball products and passing) Tj T* (machines that help with throwing and catching drills but they do not measure what the hands are) Tj T* (doing at the moment of the catch. Some general wearable sensor companies serve pro and college) Tj T* (athletes at high price points. We are not aware of a product that targets youth coaches) Tj T* (specifically with a low cost glove and drill suggestions. Our advantage is price, simplicity,) Tj T* (and focus on a single position skill. Of course a bigger company could enter this space, and we) Tj T* (have not filed any patents yet, which is a gap we know about.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marcus Delaney Otieno is our CEO and leads partnerships, he played receiver in high school and) Tj T* (has coached a youth flag league for two seasons. Priya Raghunathan-Bell is CTO and leads) Tj T* (hardware, she is a senior in electrical engineering with experience from a sensor research lab.) Tj T* (Tobias Wendelstrom leads software and the mobile app and is studying computer science. Dani) Tj T* (Kowalczyk-Reyes handles marketing and finance and is a business major who built our website. We) Tj T* (do not yet have a team member with manufacturing experience or a formal advisor from the sports) Tj T* (equipment industry, and we are looking to add one.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined the core concept, built a working prototype glove and a basic version of) Tj T* (the app, registered the company, and launched a website. We have tested the prototype with a) Tj T* (small number of players at two practices and collected early feedback which was positive though) Tj T* (the sample is small and informal. We have spent roughly 2,300 dollars to date, funded by team) Tj T* (members and a small university grant. Our next 12 months plan is to build 20 improved gloves,) Tj T* (run a pilot with 4 to 5 youth teams, get manufacturing quotes, and file a provisional patent.) Tj T* (We project revenue of about 18 thousand dollars in year one from pilot sales, growing to over) Tj T* (300 thousand dollars by year three, though these projections are based on assumptions about) Tj T* (adoption that we still need to validate. We expect to be near break even at the end of year two) Tj T* (if we keep the team lean.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to the competition for funding, mentorship and visibility. We are requesting) Tj T* (25,000 dollars in prize or seed funding which we would use for improved prototype production,) Tj T* (pilot costs, legal fees for the patent and for forming our legal entity, and basic testing.) Tj T* (Just as important, we would like to be connected to mentors with experience in consumer) Tj T* (hardware manufacturing, youth sports organizations, and early stage fundraising. We believe) Tj T* (Gridiron Glove can make quality receiver coaching available to every kid regardless of their) Tj T* (team's budget and we would be grateful for the chance to compete.) Tj ET
endstream
